{
  "contract": "native-schema-slices.md revision 3; expectations for the minimal kernel configuration",
  "slice": "2b",
  "setup": {
    "notes": [
      "Everything runs as UID 1000 in the disposable probe VM; every effect stays inside the probe or its own children",
      "prctl.set_name sets the probe thread name to 'antprobe'; an unlabeled call restores the previous name afterwards",
      "prctl.set_pdeathsig sets SIGTERM (15); an unlabeled call restores 0 afterwards",
      "prctl.get_auxv passes a 512-byte buffer; saved_auxv is 416 bytes (AT_VECTOR_SIZE 52 with IA32_EMULATION)",
      "prctl.set_mm_auxv passes {1, 2} with length 16 and is rejected for lacking CAP_SYS_RESOURCE",
      "prctl.set_vma_anon_name names a private 4096-byte mapping; CONFIG_ANON_VMA_NAME is on in the minimal profile (success) and off in the Debian profile (EINVAL); the entry field is the same either way",
      "child A sets no_new_privs, then installs a one-instruction allow-all seccomp filter (BPF_RET|BPF_K 0x7fff0000), then exits",
      "child B turns on syscall user dispatch with selector byte 0 (allow) and an empty region, then exits",
      "child C blocks SIGUSR1, calls PTRACE_TRACEME, raises SIGUSR1 (stays pending) and SIGSTOP; the parent runs the ptrace cases while it is stopped, then PTRACE_CONT lets it exit",
      "ptrace.peekdata/pokedata use a word in the child's copy of a probe global holding 0x414e54494e4f4d49; peekuser reads offset 120 (orig_rax)",
      "ptrace.setregs and setregset write back exactly the registers just read",
      "ptrace.getregset/setregset use NT_PRSTATUS with a 512-byte buffer; the kernel rewrites iov_len to 216",
      "ptrace.getsigmask_badsize passes size 4; ptrace.peeksiginfo asks for one entry from the per-thread queue (the pending SIGUSR1)",
      "ptrace.get_thread_area reads TLS index 12; ptrace.arch_prctl_get_fs passes ARCH_GET_FS as data and the output pointer as addr",
      "keyctl cases use a 'user' key 'ant:probe' with payload 'secret-payload' added by add_key to the process keyring; read_query passes a NULL buffer",
      "keyctl.dh_compute uses that key for all three parameters (CONFIG_KEY_DH_OPERATIONS=y in the minimal kernel configuration; a user key's payload is not valid DH parameters, so EINVAL); pkey_query fails because user keys have no asymmetric operations; instantiate_iov fails without an authorization key",
      "keyctl.join_session creates the session keyring 'ant-session' for the probe process only; keyctl.revoke revokes the probe key last",
      "sysfs.name uses the index returned by sysfs.index; bad_index is 9999; unknown uses option 9",
      "unknown selectors: prctl 0x7fffffff, ptrace 0x7fff, keyctl 0x7fff",
      "prctl.get_tid_address succeeds because the minimal kernel enables CONFIG_CHECKPOINT_RESTORE; the probe main thread's clear_child_tid address is compared as observed"
    ]
  },
